00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:50.000
I felt compelled to do the sign game as a historical piece because I knew the world around me was crumbling overnight. Sign painting is by no means the only industry that was wiped out by digital technology. But still, I can't help but feel extra sorry for these guys because they got their butts kicked by vinyl. Specifically the vinyl platter, which looks kind of like a big computer printer. The vinyl platters are machines that would basically tap out vinyl letters. You would program in, you know, welcome, and then it would punch out the vinyl letters and you'd weed out the vinyl with a razor blade and put the welcome letters onto the surface of your sign. When vinyl first appeared, no one would accept it.
我感到有义务把《招牌游戏》作为历史资料来创作，因为我知道我周围的世界在一夜之间分崩离析。招牌绘画绝不是唯一被数字技术淘汰的行业。但尽管如此，我还是忍不住为这些人感到格外遗憾，因为他们被乙烯基材料打败了。具体来说是乙烯基绘图仪，看起来有点像大型电脑打印机。乙烯基绘图仪是一种基本上可以刻出乙烯基字母的机器。你输入“欢迎”，它就会刻出乙烯基字母，你用剃须刀剔除多余部分，把“欢迎”字样贴到招牌表面。当乙烯基刚出现时，没人愿意接受它。

