sign painters really liked to hate in theory. And it was considered like selling out, undermining your brothers in the trade. But then slowly the guys who stubbornly clung to their brushes would call the guys who had the machines when they got in the jam. And they'd say, I'm just going to do this once, you know, but could you, you know, you give me these hundred words and then before long everybody bought into it. By the mid 1980s, sign painters were no longer in charge.
招牌画家在理论上非常讨厌的东西。它被认为是出卖行业，破坏同行。但后来，那些固执地坚持用画笔的人，在遇到麻烦时会打电话给那些有机器的人。他们会说：“我只做这一次，但你能帮我刻这100个字吗？”没过多久，每个人都接受了它。到了80年代中期，招牌画家不再是行业的主导者了。

